hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15835","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdullah, from a man of the Ansar, that he came with a black slave girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing slave to free; if you consider this one a believer I will free her. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you believe in the resurrection after death? She said: Yes. He said: Free her."
"20618","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from the Ansari, Yazid said: from a man of the Ansar, he said: I went out from my family intending the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there he was standing with a man with him facing him. I thought they had some need. He said: The Ansari said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood so long that I began to pity the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the length of standing. When he left I said: O Messenger of Allah, the man kept you standing until I began to pity you for the length of standing. He said: And you saw him? I said: Yes. He said: Do you know who he is? I said: No. He said: That is Jibril, peace be upon him. He kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir. Then he said: Had you greeted him he would have returned the greeting upon you."
